VIOLATION — compliant=false.

Breaches `rule-authoring.md` on four axes. The pole is surface-equalized with its
sibling on purpose: identical frontmatter, identical `##` heading skeleton, one
numbered clause each, the same count of `**Why:**` lines and DO blocks, a
byte-identical Wiring block and a byte-identical `## MUST NOT` section, and a size
ratio of 1.13. Every defect is in the CONTENT of that furniture, never its absence,
so a judge scoring by shape alone will get it wrong.

- MODAL BREACHED: the clause HEADING says MUST while the BODY hedges throughout —
  "should generally be bound", "it is usually preferable", "tend to be worth avoiding
  where practical", "will often be fine", "teams are encouraged to move toward". The
  load-bearing modal is what the meta-rule governs, and here the body tells the agent
  the obligation is optional.
- BLOCKED CORPUS BREACHED: the heading is PRESENT but what sits under it is an
  abstract taxonomy of error categories ("Treating expedience as a substitute for
  provenance", "Privileging presentation-layer concerns over data-lineage concerns")
  rather than the literal excuses an agent emits. A paraphrased category traps
  nothing, because no agent ever says those words.
- DO / DO-NOT BREACHED: the block is PRESENT but its two arms are structurally
  identical and differ only by the words "appropriate" and "inappropriate", which
  restate the headings. The block teaches nothing — a reader cannot tell what makes a
  source appropriate.
- WHY-LENGTH BREACHED: the MUST-1 `**Why:**` runs to four sentences, with a digression
  about asynchronous review cadence, mean time to notice, and sprint boundaries.

The `## MUST NOT` section, its `**Why:**`, the Wiring block, the frontmatter and the
`## Origin` are shared with the compliant pole and are NOT findings — a judge
reporting a defect there has keyed on the wrong surface. The deferred Phase-2
detector is likewise shared and sanctioned.
